<section class="panel panel-pad mt-6" aria-labelledby="f1-benchmark-title">
  <h2 id="f1-benchmark-title" class="font-semibold">Precision / Recall / F1: held-out sample</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">
    <%= num(benchmark.fetch("test_cards")) %> held-out cards; training: <%= num(benchmark.fetch("training_cards")) %>.
    Settings were chosen on a separate validation set. Matching texts and model families were excluded from training by fixed heuristics.
    This is a local check on the pilot's historical data, not an external evaluation.
  </p>
  <dl class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-4">
    <% candidate = benchmark.fetch("candidate") %>
    <% [["Macro F1", candidate.fetch("macro_f1")],
        ["Precision (micro)", candidate.fetch("totals").fetch("precision")],
        ["Recall (micro)", candidate.fetch("totals").fetch("recall")],
        ["Coverage of labelled fields", candidate.fetch("totals").fetch("coverage")]].each do |label, value| %>
      <div><dt class="text-sm text-muted"><%= label %></dt><dd class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold tabular-nums"><%= format("%.4f", value) %></dd></div>
    <% end %>
  </dl>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
    Macro F1 before the improvement: <%= format("%.4f", benchmark.fetch("baseline").fetch("macro_f1")) %>.
    Including labelled fields outside the category's list: <%= format("%.4f", candidate.fetch("macro_f1_all_labels")) %>.
    Suggestions from other products' statistics require a person to check them.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted">
    The metrics come from one partially labelled sample: unlabelled values are not checked.
    This shows the frozen evaluation model; the shipped production model was then further trained on all pilot cards.
    Protocol, predictions and SHA-256: results/f1-max/ and docs/f1-max-2026-10-25.md in the project archive.
  </p>
</section>
